    "training_evaluation": "In PurchaseDataset.__getitem__(self, index), replace arbitrary reconstruction with t = np.random.randint(1, len(history)), target = int(history[t]), and context = history[:t], preserving existing variable names, function signatures, dataset eligibility, and the (sequence, candidates) return format; retain earlier occurrences of target because they are legitimate past interactions. Apply the existing truncation mixture, order-preserving subsampling, 15% context dropout with its nonempty safeguard, and right-aligned padding only after selecting the prefix, while preserving 64 uniformly sampled training negatives excluded against self.known[index], which contains the complete training history, including the existing policy permitting duplicate training negatives. Keep unchanged AttentiveSimilarity, dimensions, attention normalization, biases, model dropout, sampled cross-entropy, regularization, AdamW, batch size, DataLoader configuration, EPOCHS with environment default 200, PATIENCE, validation cadence, HR@10/NDCG@10 checkpoint selection, and per-category time limits; this isolates temporal supervision despite the prior similar failure. Add lightweight deterministic sampler checks covering target boundaries, repeated items, two-interaction histories, nonempty augmented contexts, full-history negative exclusion, and unchanged output shapes, restoring RNG states afterward; compare authoritative host macro HR@10 against 0.4462 and category scores against their current values, treating 0.46 as an experimental target rather than an expected result. Preserve preprocessing seed 0, training and evaluation seeds 42, supplied splits, all four categories and dataset_name routing, DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], trial-local artifacts, single-GPU execution, the shared 43,200 GPU-second search budget, and the existing predictor writer and inference behavior because architecture is unchanged; retain the pinned 200-user/category validation protocol with 99 unique negatives and no hidden-test access, external data, pretrained weights, or host-evaluator changes."
